invariant: INV-11
file: record.c
catches: aes_suite_test
reason: KeyUpdate rekeys an AES-GCM direction through rec_dir_init, which
  derives a 32-byte ChaCha20 key, so the first KeyUpdate switches the
  AEAD the connection runs. Both ends of a chapulin pair rekey the same
  way and still open what the other seals; a peer that kept AES-GCM
  fails the next record. test_key_update_keeps_suite keys its reader on
  its own from the updated secret.

--- old
    REC_DIR_INIT_SUITE(d, secret, d->suite);
--- new
    rec_dir_init(d, secret);
